{
  "policy": "policy.json",
  "note": "Each case is a call and the expected answer under policy.json. `reasonPrefix` is compared with startsWith. `description` absent means the harness gave none. Case 21 needs confusable folding (policy.md, section 3), which session 0's Rust fold_text does not do yet. Cases 22 to 33 were added by integration w1 to pin what all three matchers agree on (policy.md, sections 2 to 4). Cases 34 to 45 were added by integration w1 after its security pass (findings S1, S4, S7 and S10): quotes, globs, git config files, continued lines and harness folders. Case 7 changed and cases 46 to 51 were added by integration w2 for finding S5: a Claude Code plugin's server keeps its whole name (plugin_<plugin>_<server>); a rule on a bare server it could be narrows it and never allows it; an mcp__ name with a second run of __ that servers does not settle asks instead of allowing.",
  "cases": [
    { "id": 1, "call": { "tool": "mcp__exa__search", "harness": "pi", "inputText": "{\"query\":\"rust\"}" },
      "expect": { "action": "allow", "normalizedTool": "exa/search", "reasonPrefix": "rule" } },
    { "id": 2, "call": { "tool": "mcp_exa_search", "harness": "gemini", "inputText": "" },
      "expect": { "action": "allow", "normalizedTool": "exa/search", "reasonPrefix": "rule" } },
